   Guenther, Wanda Maria Rizzo and Ribeiro, Helena and de Assuncao, Joao
   Vicente},
Title = {Risk perception: a field of interest for the interface between
   environment, health, and sustainability},
Journal = {SAUDE E SOCIEDADE},
Year = {2015},
Volume = {24},
Number = {4},
Pages = {1217-1231},
Month = {OCT-DEC},
Abstract = {In this article, the authors discuss the complex field of per more
   specifically of the per of risk, drawing on a theoretical and
   methodological essay that seeks to stress the importance of risk
   perception in studies related to the interface environment, health and
   sustainability, Recognizing that social and cultural elements shape in
   direct and indirect is individual's perceptions of different risks, the
   authors flag that studies in this field can point out specific
   interests, values, and points of conflicts that exist in the arenas and
   offer insights that would help decision makers improve their decision
   making processes with greater involvement of society, In addition to
   risk perception, the article also discusses examples of investigations
   conducted by the authors focusing on environmental perception, Searching
   for a critical perspective to cover the subject, the authors recognize
   the need to understand, in environmental and societal processes, the
   setting of socio-environmental risks and how they are perceived,},
